# Private Rooms & Fanout (Phase 5B.1)

- Laravel alone authorizes room membership. Node never queries PostgreSQL for ACL.
- Room access requires a one-use REST grant (`WS_ROOM_GRANT_REDIS_PREFIX`), redeemed with atomic `GETDEL` inside an already-authenticated socket. Never accept client `player_id` / open `room_id` as authority.
- Bind grant `user_id` to the authenticated socket identity before `room.subscribed`.
- Fanout only to: (1) `target_user_id` personal sockets, or (2) sockets with an active authorized room subscription for `target_room_id`.
- Redis Pub/Sub is best-effort. Clients must rehydrate via REST. Fail closed for private fanout when Redis is unavailable.
- No combat calculations, XP, or battle outcomes in Node.
- On `room.subscription.revoked` / room close, drop local subscriptions.
